# Governance workspace context

Read root `AGENTS.md` once, then the nearest scoped `AGENTS.md` for changed files.
The current product serves financial-institution governance professionals through
issue context, evidence, review decisions, and history. Do not assume an old phase
handoff or this editor configuration authorizes new work.

Load context progressively:

- Governance demo/shared UI: `apps/governance-console/AGENTS.md` and
  `docs/governance-redesign.md`.
- Connected runtime/gateway: `apps/governance-live/AGENTS.md` and
  `docs/governance-integration.md`.
- Backend: `services/<service>/AGENTS.md`, then the relevant phase spec.
- Envelopes, idempotency, CDC, outbox: `docs/data-flow.md` and `contracts/kafka/`.
- Setup: `docs/quickstart.md`; operational gotchas and historical gates:
  `docs/agent-guide.md`.

Preserve synthetic/demo versus connected-development labels, PostgreSQL review
history versus ledger evidence, and explicit verification. Run the checks for the
changed path; do not describe a build as a running-service or browser check.

Do not read private session transcripts, other agents' terminal history, or live
evaluation answer keys as implementation context. Run the requested eval tools
instead of reading their answer material. Avoid rereading unchanged instructions.
Use available native tools; do not install or reactivate a harness, change global
plugins, or write personal memory based on a repository rule.

Parallel work needs disjoint ownership and independent review; keep shared-state
mutations ordered. Use worktree/Compose rules only when relevant. For an explicitly
active corporate site program, preserve its scoped handoff and evidence gates;
historical program records do not expand authority.
